      "retrieved": "2026-10-12",
      "revision": 1358027732,
      "text": "Ugni molinae, commonly known as Chilean guava berry, or strawberry myrtle, is a shrub native to Chile and adjacent regions of southern Argentina. The local Spanish name is murta, and the Mapuche Native American name is \"uñi\". It is in the same botanical family as the guava, in Myrtaceae."
